Azure Data Factory – Blob to Azure SQL Pipeline
Overview

This project demonstrates an end-to-end data ingestion pipeline using Azure Data Factory. The pipeline reads CSV data from Azure Blob Storage and loads it into an Azure SQL Database table using Copy Activity.

Architecture Components

Azure Blob Storage (CSV Source)

Azure Data Factory

Linked Services

Dataset Configuration

Copy Data Activity

Azure SQL Database (Sink)

Linked Services Created

Azure SQL Database

Name: AzureSQLClinicalResearchDB_LS

Authentication: SQL Authentication

Integration Runtime: AutoResolveIntegrationRuntime

Azure Blob Storage

Name: ClinicalResearchSA_LS

Authentication: Account Key

Integration Runtime: AutoResolveIntegrationRuntime

Dataset Configuration

Source Dataset:

Name: Blob_Dept

Format: DelimitedText (CSV)

File Path: data/example.csv

First row as header: Enabled

Sink Dataset:

Name: AzSQL_Dept

Table: dbo.Dept

Auto Create Table: Enabled

Pipeline Implementation

Activity Used: Copy Data

Source: Azure Blob CSV

Sink: Azure SQL Database

Schema Import: None

Table Creation: Automatic

Outcome

CSV data successfully loaded into Azure SQL Database

Table dbo.Dept auto-created

Pipeline validated and debugged successfully

